  "id": "rebound-phenomenon",
  "term": "rebound phenomenon",
  "definition": "In this context, a rebound phenomenon is a rise in brain alpha activity that continues after alternating current stimulation has ended. It is used to describe an aftereffect that reflects a post-stimulation return or overshoot in activity, rather than ongoing synchronization of brain rhythms to the stimulation itself.",
